# Lane scratch (dig-app#178/#175). A lane anchors its branch with a stub commit so a
# watchdog death leaves something to resume from; the anchor is working state, never
# product. Ignoring the shapes stops `git add -A` sweeping one up. It is only half the
# fix -- it cannot stop `git add -f` and cannot see an already-tracked file, so
# scripts/check-scratch-paths.py gates the tracked tree as well.
.lane-*
LANE.md
LANE-*.md
.loop/

# Python bytecode from the scripts/ CI guards.
__pycache__/

# gitnexus analyze writes these as a side effect; they are tooling output, not this repo.
.lane/
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
.claude/skills/gitnexus/

# Lane-private scratch (dig-app#329 batch)
.own.md
.pr-body.md
